cription></item><item><title>Barebone Media PC - living room computer gets the retro VCR treatment</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/barebone-media-pc-living-room-computer/</link><pubDate>Tue, 03 Mar 2009 14:02:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/barebone-media-pc-living-room-computer/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Another thing for my wishlist&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;div style="margin: 0px 2px; padding-top: 1px; background-color: #c3d9ff; font-size: 1px !important; line-height: 0px !important;"&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="margin: 0px 1px; padding-top: 1px; background-color: #c3d9ff; font-size: 1px !important; line-height: 0px !important;"&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="padding: 4px; background-color: #c3d9ff;"&gt;&lt;h3 style="margin:0px 3px;font-family:sans-serif"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="margin: 0px 1px; padding-top: 1px; background-color: #c3d9ff; font-size: 1px !important; line-height: 0px !important;"&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="margin: 0px 2px; padding-top: 1px; background-color: #c3d9ff; font-size: 1px !important; line-height: 0px !important;"&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="font-family:sans-serif;overflow:auto;width:100%;margin: 0px 10px"&gt;&lt;h2 style="margin: 0.25em 0 0 0"&gt;&lt;div class=""&gt;&lt;a href="http://www.redferret.net/?p=13218"&gt;Barebone Media PC - living room computer gets the retro VCR treatment&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h2&gt; &lt;div style="margin-bottom: 0.5em"&gt;via &lt;a href="http://www.redferret.net/" class="f"&gt;The Red Ferret Journal&lt;/a&gt; by Nigel on 03/03/09&lt;/div&gt; &lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt="Barebonesmediapc3" src="http://www.redferret.net/wp-content/uploads/2009/03/barebonesmediapc3-small2.jpg" border="0" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;This Barebone Media PC comes with an Intel motherboard, 7.1 surround sound, digital TV card, WiFi card and 1GB of RAM in [&amp;hellip;]&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr noshade="" style="margin:0;height:1px"&gt; &lt;p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Samsung NC20, one for the wish list.</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/samsung-nc20-one-for-wish-list/</link><pubDate>Thu, 05 Feb 2009 14:24:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/samsung-nc20-one-for-wish-list/</guid><description>&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; 3 of this post&amp;rsquo;s 4 links are now broken — mostly dead 2008–2013 feed-syndication infrastructure (FeedBurner, Gawker, AOL&amp;rsquo;s old blog network, Pheedo, Yahoo Pipes). Left as originally published.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt; More drool worthy kit, just wish I could justify getting a Netbook o_0&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;h1&gt;&lt;a href="http://www2.blogger.com/%PostURL"&gt;Samsung NC20, 3G NC10 now available for pre-order in the UK&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;h3&gt;02-05-2009&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;div align="center"&gt;&lt;a href="http://www.shop.bt.com/learn-more/computers/samsung-netbook-range-4985.html"&gt;&lt;img src="http://www.blogcdn.com/www.engadget.com/media/2009/01/1-14-09-samsung_nc20_10.jpg" alt="" border="0" hspace="4" vspace="4" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt; The Russians have already declared their love, and soon you'll be able to get your mitts on the &lt;a href="http://www.engadget.com/2009/01/29/samsung-nc20-sees-foreign-review-universal-appreciation/"&gt;Samsung N20&lt;/a&gt; and see for yourself what all the fuss is about. It's now available for pre-order from UK retailer BT Shop, priced at &lt;span class="lprice" id="ctl00_mainContent_MerchPanels_rptProductListMerch_ctl00_spnPrice"&gt;£390.98 ($565) VAT included, with a white model&lt;/span&gt; due out in February and a black iteration in March. Both models sport a 12.1-inch WXGA display, Windowx XP Home Edition, 1.3GHz VIA Nano U225 CPU processor, 1GB RAM, 160GB HDD, Bluetooth, 3-in-1 card reader, 1.3 megapixel camera, and a 6 Cell battery -- no SSD option at the moment. Additionally, the shop is also showing a new NC10 equipped with HSDPA coming next month for &lt;span class="lprice" id="ctl00_mainContent_HotDeal_rptProductListMerch_ctl00_spnPrice"&gt;£416.63 ($602) with&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="price" id="ctl00_mainContent_HotDeal_rptProductListMerch_ctl00_spnVat"&gt; VAT, which is &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lprice" id="ctl00_mainContent_HotDeal_rptProductListMerch_ctl00_spnPrice"&gt;£107 ($154) more than its non-3G equivalent.&lt;/span&gt; Not to worry, US readers, we're sure Sammy will be asking for your Benjamins soon enough.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;[Thanks, Darpan]</description></item><item><title>DSTL1 Android Smartphone Is Battlestar Galactica's iPhone [Android]</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/dstl1-android-smartphone-is-battlestar/</link><pubDate>Wed, 28 Jan 2009 12:31:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/dstl1-android-smartphone-is-battlestar/</guid><description>&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; 6 of this post&amp;rsquo;s 8 links are now broken — mostly dead 2008–2013 feed-syndication infrastructure (FeedBurner, Gawker, AOL&amp;rsquo;s old blog network, Pheedo, Yahoo Pipes). Left as originally published.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;I wish I hadn&amp;rsquo;t just renewed my phone contract now. My LG Renoir now looks like the ugly cousin.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;div style="margin: 0px 2px; padding-top: 1px; background-color: #c3d9ff; font-size: 1px !important; line-height: 0px !important;"&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="margin: 0px 1px; padding-top: 1px; background-color: #c3d9ff; font-size: 1px !important; line-height: 0px !important;"&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="padding: 4px; background-color: #c3d9ff;"&gt;&lt;h3 style="margin:0px 3px;font-family:sans-serif"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="margin: 0px 1px; padding-top: 1px; background-color: #c3d9ff; font-size: 1px !important; line-height: 0px !important;"&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="margin: 0px 2px; padding-top: 1px; background-color: #c3d9ff; font-size: 1px !important; line-height: 0px !important;"&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="font-family:sans-serif;overflow:auto;width:100%;margin: 0px 10px"&gt;&lt;h2 style="margin: 0.25em 0 0 0"&gt;&lt;div class=""&gt;&lt;a href="http://feeds.gawker.com/~r/gizmodo/full/~3/h_huBqZJHUw/dstl1-android-smartphone-is-battlestar-galacticas-iphone"&gt;DSTL1 Android Smartphone Is Battlestar Galactica&amp;rsquo;s iPhone [Android]&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h2&gt; &lt;div style="margin-bottom: 0.5em"&gt;via &lt;a href="http://gizmodo.com/" class="f"&gt;Gizmodo&lt;/a&gt; by Jesus Diaz on 27/01/09&lt;/div&gt; &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="http://cache.gawker.com/assets/images/gizmodo/2009/01/dstl1_pretty.jpg" width="804" height="518" style="display:block;float:none" /&gt;This is the Android-based, 3-inch Sharp touchscreen, General Mobile DSTL1. And it is everything the T-Mobile isn&amp;rsquo;t: A stunning design &lt;i&gt;and&lt;/i&gt; features combination that may convince regular consumers to choose the Android platform over iPhone.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Take two cameras into the shower?</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/alastair-montgomery-asked-us-to-send/</link><pubDate>Thu, 22 Jan 2009 13:49:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/alastair-montgomery-asked-us-to-send/</guid><description>&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; 2 of this post&amp;rsquo;s 7 links are now broken — mostly dead 2008–2013 feed-syndication infrastructure (FeedBurner, Gawker, AOL&amp;rsquo;s old blog network, Pheedo, Yahoo Pipes). Left as originally published.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt; Some cool video cameras which are muscling in on the stills market. I'm a sucker for multi function devices, why carry a stills &amp;amp; video camera. Now they just have to integrate a MP4 player and cell phone into it. Watch this space.......&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Eee PC Touch Demo</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/eee-pc-touch-demo/</link><pubDate>Tue, 20 Jan 2009 11:36:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/eee-pc-touch-demo/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;How cool does this look?&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;object height="344" width="425"&gt;&lt;param name="movie" value="http://www.youtube.com/v/5mvtU4xZPvQ&amp;amp;color1=0xb1b1b1&amp;amp;color2=0xcfcfcf&amp;amp;hl=en&amp;amp;feature=player_embedded&amp;amp;fs=1"&gt;&lt;param name="allowFullScreen" value="true"&gt;&lt;embed src="http://www.youtube.com/v/5mvtU4xZPvQ&amp;amp;color1=0xb1b1b1&amp;amp;color2=0xcfcfcf&amp;amp;hl=en&amp;amp;feature=player_embedded&amp;amp;fs=1" type="application/x-shockwave-flash" allowfullscreen="true" height="344" width="425"&gt;&lt;/embed&gt;&lt;/object&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;span style="font-style: italic;"&gt;Having trouble figuring out how a touchscreen Eee PC could fit into your life? No worries, ASUS just did all the heavy synaptic lifting for you with the release of a near 6-minute video showing its new Eee PC Touch UI. A &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a style="font-style: italic;" href="http://www.engadget.com/2009/01/06/eee-pc-t91-convertible-tablet-lives/"&gt;UI teased at CES&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style="font-style: italic;"&gt; and built specifically for ASUS&amp;rsquo; new touchcreen Eees. All in all it makes a pretty case for why you should pick up a new &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a style="font-style: italic;" href="http://www.engadget.com/2009/01/08/asus-eee-pc-t91-and-t101h-touchscreen-tablet-hands-on/"&gt;Eee PC T91 or T101H&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style="font-style: italic;"&gt; convertible tablet later this year. Let&amp;rsquo;s just hope the processor can cope.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:85%;"&gt;Originally posted at &lt;a href="http://www.engadget.com/2009/01/20/video-sexy-eee-pc-touch-ui-demonstrated/"&gt;Engadget&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;a href="http://meekgonkey.blogspot.com/"&gt;Doodle&amp;rsquo;s Geek Monkey&lt;/a&gt; by &lt;a href="http://twitter.com/alastair_hm"&gt;Alastair Montgomery&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Phillips Making 21:9 TV</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/phillips-making-219-tv/</link><pubDate>Tue, 20 Jan 2009 08:46:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/phillips-making-219-tv/</guid><description>&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; 1 of this post&amp;rsquo;s 6 links are now broken — mostly dead 2008–2013 feed-syndication infrastructure (FeedBurner, Gawker, AOL&amp;rsquo;s old blog network, Pheedo, Yahoo Pipes). Left as originally published.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Something to add to your wish list?&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;div style="margin: 0px 2px; padding-top: 1px; background-color: rgb(195, 217, 255); font-size: 1px ! important; line-height: 0px ! important;"&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="margin: 0px 1px; padding-top: 1px; background-color: rgb(195, 217, 255); font-size: 1px ! important; line-height: 0px ! important;"&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="padding: 4px; background-color: rgb(195, 217, 255);"&gt;&lt;h3 style="margin: 0px 3px; font-family: sans-serif;"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="margin: 0px 1px; padding-top: 1px; background-color: rgb(195, 217, 255); font-size: 1px ! important; line-height: 0px ! important;"&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="margin: 0px 2px; padding-top: 1px; background-color: rgb(195, 217, 255); font-size: 1px ! important; line-height: 0px ! important;"&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="margin: 0px 10px; overflow: auto; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;"&gt;&lt;h2 style="margin: 0.25em 0pt 0pt;"&gt;&lt;div class=""&gt;&lt;a href="http://www.geekologie.com/2009/01/sure_why_not_phillips_making_2.php"&gt;Sure, Why Not?: Phillips Making 21:9 TV&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h2&gt; &lt;div style="margin-bottom: 0.5em;"&gt;via &lt;a href="http://www.geekologie.com/" class="f"&gt;Geekologie - Gadgets, Gizmos, and Awesome&lt;/a&gt; on 19/01/09&lt;/div&gt; &lt;span style="display: inline;"&gt;&lt;img alt="cinema.jpg" src="http://www.geekologie.com/2009/01/19/cinema.jpg" width="450" height="395" /&gt;&lt;/span&gt; The 56&amp;quot; Phillips Cinema Widescreen LCD is a 21:9 &lt;a href="http://www.geekologie.com/2009/01/australian_fixes_plasma_tv_wit.php"&gt;television&lt;/a&gt; hitting the streets of selected countries&lt;a href="http://www.geekologie.com/2009/01/obama_requests_extension_for_a.php"&gt; next month&lt;/a&gt;. If you want one you can pay an arm and a kidney and watch movies in the proper 21:9 aspect ratio without black barring it. If you don&amp;rsquo;t want one, forget you ever read this and save that precious brain-space for something useful. Like a tv theme song! Which reminds me &amp;ndash; &amp;ldquo;thank you for being a friend&amp;hellip;&amp;rdquo; Haha, marinate on that one all afternoon, suckers! &lt;a href="http://technabob.com/blog/2009/01/19/philips-cinema-21-9-ultra-widescreen/"&gt;philips cinema 21:9 ultra widescreen perfect for movie snobs&lt;/a&gt; [technabob] Thanks to Julian, who who thought about getting one until he realized he owned a movie theater. An &lt;em&gt;adult&lt;/em&gt; movie theater. No, that&amp;rsquo;s not creepy.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;div style="margin: 0px 2px; padding-top: 1px; background-color: rgb(195, 217, 255); font-size: 1px ! important; line-height: 0px ! important;"&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="margin: 0px 1px; padding-top: 1px; background-color: rgb(195, 217, 255); font-size: 1px ! important; line-height: 0px ! important;"&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="padding: 4px; background-color: rgb(195, 217, 255);"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="margin: 0px 1px; padding-top: 1px; background-color: rgb(195, 217, 255); font-size: 1px ! important; line-height: 0px ! important;"&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="margin: 0px 2px; padding-top: 1px; background-color: rgb(195, 217, 255); font-size: 1px ! important; line-height: 0px ! important;"&gt; &lt;/div&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Neuros Link Media PC - stream multimedia around and about</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/neuros-link-media-pc-stream-multimedia/</link><pubDate>Sat, 10 Jan 2009 20:04:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/neuros-link-media-pc-stream-multimedia/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Something else to add to my wish list.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;div style="margin: 0px 2px; padding-top: 1px; background-color: #c3d9ff; font-size: 1px !important; line-height: 0px !important;"&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="margin: 0px 1px; padding-top: 1px; background-color: #c3d9ff; font-size: 1px !important; line-height: 0px !important;"&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="padding: 4px; background-color: #c3d9ff;"&gt;&lt;h3 style="margin:0px 3px;font-family:sans-serif"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="margin: 0px 1px; padding-top: 1px; background-color: #c3d9ff; font-size: 1px !important; line-height: 0px !important;"&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="margin: 0px 2px; padding-top: 1px; background-color: #c3d9ff; font-size: 1px !important; line-height: 0px !important;"&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="font-family:sans-serif;overflow:auto;width:100%;margin: 0px 10px"&gt;&lt;h2 style="margin: 0.25em 0 0 0"&gt;&lt;div class=""&gt;&lt;a href="http://www.redferret.net/?p=12401"&gt;Neuros Link Media PC - stream multimedia around and about&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h2&gt; &lt;div style="margin-bottom: 0.5em"&gt;via &lt;a href="http://www.redferret.net/" class="f"&gt;The Red Ferret Journal&lt;/a&gt; by Nigel on 09/01/09&lt;/div&gt; &lt;img alt="Neuroslink" src="http://www.redferret.net/wp-content/uploads/2008/12/neuroslink-small.jpg" border="0" /&gt; The Neuros Link Media PC is an open source powered home entertainment computer which is designed to make you feel all [&amp;hellip;]&lt;hr noshade="" style="margin:0;he