x-DMC-LX3/p1"&gt;Panasonic Lumix DMC-LX3 Review - Digital Camera Reviews - TrustedReviews&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;My new wishlist camera &lt;em&gt;drool&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;a href="http://meekgonkey.blogspot.com/"&gt;Doodle&amp;rsquo;s Geek Monkey&lt;/a&gt; by &lt;a href="http://twitter.com/alastair_hm"&gt;Alastair Montgomery&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Baumhauser : Amazing Prefab Treehouses by Baumraum</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/baumhauser-amazing-prefab-treehouses-by/</link><pubDate>Tue, 14 Oct 2008 18:00:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/baumhauser-amazing-prefab-treehouses-by/</guid><description>&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; 2 of this post&amp;rsquo;s 18 links are now broken — mostly dead 2008–2013 feed-syndication infrastructure (FeedBurner, Gawker, AOL&amp;rsquo;s old blog network, Pheedo, Yahoo Pipes). Left as originally published.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="http://www.bloglines.com/"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;I always wanted a tree house as a kid, this looks like an idea one :) &lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt; &lt;table width="100%"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;a name="base10815999"&gt; &lt;/a&gt;&lt;table id="table10815999" bg cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0" width="100%" style="color:#bde0ed;"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt; &lt;td rowspan="2"&gt; &lt;table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;span class="blogtitle"&gt;&lt;a href="http://freshome.com/"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Furniture, Interior Design, Architecture, Decor and Home &amp;amp; House Design&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Freshome is the perfect source of inspiration for home design, furniture inspiration, interior design, architecture, advices and tips. &lt;/td&gt; &lt;/tr&gt; &lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt; &lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; &lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;a name="base10815999"&gt; &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;div id="items10815999" style="display: block;"&gt; &lt;table width="100%"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr bgcolor="#ffffff"&gt; &lt;td&gt; &lt;table width="100%"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;h2&gt;&lt;a title="Site: Furniture, Interior Design, Architecture, Decor and Home &amp;amp; House Design" href="http://feeds.feedburner.com/%7Er/FreshInspirationForYourHome/%7E3/414834587/"&gt;Baumhauser : Amazing Prefab Treehouses by Baumraum&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt; By Alex Ion on trees &lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Here&amp;rsquo;s a good question. What you get when an architect, a landscape architect, an arbologist, and a craftsman get together and work on something new? An amazing prefab treehouses dubbed Baumhauser. Of course that&amp;rsquo;s not the only thing they can come up with, but some guys in Germany did it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="text-align: center;"&gt;&lt;img class="size-full wp-image-5348 aligncenter" title="Baumraum Prefab Treehouses" src="http://freshome.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/10/baumraum-prefab-treehouses-1.jpg" alt="" width="490" height="267" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;These modern natural tree houses may be the solution to the whole economic system we&amp;rsquo;re going through these days. Yes, we could start living in trees and that&amp;rsquo;s because &lt;a href="http://www.baumraum.de/" target="_blank"&gt;Baumraum&lt;/a&gt; designed the Baumhauser with treespaces that can be outfitted with &amp;ldquo;sitting and sleeping benches, storage spaces, a mini-kitchen, heating, glass windows, lighting, as well as a sound system for multimedia&amp;rdquo;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="text-align: center;"&gt;&lt;img class="size-full wp-image-5349 aligncenter" title="Baumraum Prefab Treehouses" src="http://freshome.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/10/baumraum-prefab-treehouses-2.jpg" alt="" width="490" height="267" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="text-align: center;"&gt;&lt;img class="size-full wp-image-5350 aligncenter" title="Baumraum Prefab Treehouses" src="http://freshome.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/10/baumraum-prefab-treehouses-3.jpg" alt="" width="490" height="267" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="text-align: center;"&gt;&lt;img class="size-full wp-image-5351 aligncenter" title="Baumraum Prefab Treehouses" src="http://freshome.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/10/baumraum-prefab-treehouses-4.jpg" alt="" width="490" height="267" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Built from larch and Douglas pine it can virtually be put in every tree out there. Is that the &lt;a href="http://freshome.com/2008/01/08/top-8-most-amazing-tree-houses/" target="_blank"&gt;coolest treehouse&lt;/a&gt; you&amp;rsquo;ve ever seen? - via &lt;a href="http://gliving.tv/architecture-design/baumhauser-from-baumraum" target="_blank"&gt;Gliving&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="text-align: center;"&gt;&lt;img class="size-full wp-image-5352 aligncenter" title="Baumraum Prefab Treehouses" src="http://freshome.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/10/baumraum-prefab-treehouses-5.jpg" alt="" width="490" height="267" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-5353" title="Baumraum Prefab Treehouses" src="http://freshome.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/10/baumraum-prefab-treehouses-6.jpg" alt="" width="490" height="267" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-5354" title="Baumraum Prefab Treehouses" src="http://freshome.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/10/baumraum-prefab-treehouses-7.jpg" alt="" width="490" height="267" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-5355" title="Baumraum Prefab Treehouses" src="http://freshome.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/10/baumraum-prefab-treehouses-8.jpg" alt="" width="490" height="267" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-5356" title="Baumraum Prefab Treehouses" src="http://freshome.com/wp-content/uploads/2008/10/baumraum-prefab-treehouses-9.jpg" alt="" width="490" height="267" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;a&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="http://freshome.com/2008/10/08/baumhauser-amazing-prefab-treehouses-by-baumraum/" target="Bwindow"&gt;Baumhauser : Amazing Prefab Treehouses by Baumraum&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="http://feeds.feedburner.com/%7Ea/FreshInspirationForYourHome?a=0dQMgU" target="Bwindow"&gt;&lt;img src="http://feeds.feedburner.com/%7Ea/FreshInspirationForYourHome?i=0dQMgU" border="0" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; &lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; &lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt; &lt;/div&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; &lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Yama Vac Pot</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/yama-vac-pot/</link><pubDate>Thu, 02 Oct 2008 09:27:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/yama-vac-pot/</guid><description>&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; 10 of this post&amp;rsquo;s 20 links are now broken — mostly dead 2008–2013 feed-syndication infrastructure (FeedBurner, Gawker, AOL&amp;rsquo;s old blog network, Pheedo, Yahoo Pipes). Left as originally published.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="http://www.bloglines.com/"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;I want one, love the retro look, maybe its the coffee geek in me. &lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt; &lt;table width="100%"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;a name="base9477167"&gt; &lt;/a&gt;&lt;table id="table9477167" bg cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0" width="100%" style="color:#bde0ed;"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt; &lt;td rowspan="2"&gt; &lt;table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;span class="blogtitle"&gt;&lt;a href="http://pipes.yahoo.com/pipes/pipe.info?_id=8IsQFi282xG5FaTJJjBjOg"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Life GH Com&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Pipes Output &lt;/td&gt; &lt;/tr&gt; &lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt; &lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; &lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;a name="base9477167"&gt; &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;div id="items9477167" style="display: block;"&gt; &lt;table width="100%"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr bgcolor="#ffffff"&gt; &lt;td&gt; &lt;table width="100%"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;h2&gt;&lt;a title="Site: Life GH Com" href="http://feeds.feedburner.com/%7Er/CoolTools/%7E3/408386516/003072.php"&gt;Yama Vac Pot&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt; In Kitchen &lt;p&gt; &lt;img src="http://www.kk.org/cooltools/yama-vac-pot-sm.jpg" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This glass siphon brews a smooth, strong cup of coffee with little to no bitterness. I started using one recently and right away the taste was just awesome. It&amp;rsquo;s really an excellent, efficient brewing method, provided you want to get involved. You put the water in the bottom &amp;ldquo;globe&amp;rdquo; and coffee grounds in the top, then put the bottom unit on the stove with a medium flame. Once the water begins to boil, you place the top globe onto the bottom one, which allows the water to travel into the top chamber to begin brewing the coffee. You give the coffee a quick stir, cover the top with the lid and after maybe a minute, take the whole unit off the burner. As it cools, the coffee is siphoned back down into the bottom through a cloth filter, which helps extract most of the moisture and flavor from the grinds via gravity, rather than the force of a standard French press (step-by-step photos are available at &lt;a rel="nofollow" target="_blank" href="http://stumptowncoffee.com/"&gt;Stumptown&amp;rsquo;s site&lt;/a&gt; &amp;ndash; click on the link to &amp;ldquo;brewing guide&amp;rdquo;). You can also see vac pots in use at the &lt;a rel="nofollow" target="_blank" href="http://bluebottlecoffee.net/"&gt;Blue Bottle&lt;/a&gt; location near the Chronicle building in San Francisco. The $20,000 system they have there is just a fancy vac pot. While researching a coffee maker called the &lt;a rel="nofollow" target="_blank" href="http://www.wired.com/gadgets/miscellaneous/magazine/16-08/mf_clover"&gt;Clover&lt;/a&gt;, I went from addict to obsessive, so in addition to the vac pot, now I kind of want a &lt;a rel="nofollow" target="_blank" href="http://www.chemexcoffeemaker.com/"&gt;Chemex&lt;/a&gt; and I definitely want a Burr grinder; once you notice the difference in taste, it&amp;rsquo;s easy to get sucked in. Personally, I love this method. If you spend money on good beans, it&amp;rsquo;s well worth the extra effort to brew a cup that tastes that much better.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;ndash; Mathew Honan&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Here&amp;rsquo;s a video of the final siphon process. &amp;ndash;sl&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div&gt; &lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Yama Vac Pot&lt;br /&gt;$44&lt;br /&gt;Available from &lt;a rel="nofollow" target="_blank" href="http://www.amazon.com/dp/B000NBK22W/ref=nosim/kkorg-20"&gt;Amazon&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Manufactured by &lt;a rel="nofollow" target="_blank" href="http://www.yama.nl/"&gt;Yama Products&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt; Related Entries:&lt;br /&gt;&lt;a rel="nofollow" target="_blank" href="http://www.kk.org/cooltools/archives/002681.php"&gt;Popcorn Popper as Coffee Roaster&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a rel="nofollow" target="_blank" href="http://www.kk.org/cooltools/archives/002932.php"&gt;Scoop Clip&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a rel="nofollow" target="_blank" href="http://www.kk.org/cooltools/archives/002954.php"&gt;Best home chemistry lab book&lt;/a&gt;&lt;div class="feedflare"&gt;&lt;a rel="nofollow" target="_blank" href="http://feeds.feedburner.com/%7Ef/CoolTools?a=WtpLM"&gt;&lt;img src="http://feeds.feedburner.com/%7Ef/CoolTools?i=WtpLM" border="0" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a rel="nofollow" target="_blank" href="http://feeds.feedburner.com/%7Ef/CoolTools?a=g562M"&gt;&lt;img src="http://feeds.feedburner.com/%7Ef/CoolTools?i=g562M" border="0" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a rel="nofollow" target="_blank" href="http://feeds.feedburner.com/%7Ef/CoolTools?a=b9fqM"&gt;&lt;img src="http://feeds.feedburner.com/%7Ef/CoolTools?i=b9fqM" border="0" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;img src="http://feeds.feedburner.com/%7Er/CoolTools/%7E4/408386516" height="1" width="1" /&gt; &lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" width="100%"&gt; &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td align="left" valign="top"&gt; &lt;br /&gt;&lt;/td&gt; &lt;td align="right" valign="top"&gt;&lt;br /&gt; &lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; &lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; &lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt; &lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; &lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt; &lt;/div&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt; &lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>